# Pipeline OS — Cursor app

Pipeline is the governance kernel. Cursor Desktop/Agents Window is the normal
Cursor runtime; CLI agents, SDK agents, API keys, and relay daemons are not
required.

For non-trivial work, inspect fresh smoke, recent Git history, scoped status,
and relevant mailbox bodies. Durable state beats chat memory.

Default posture is readiness. A named seat exists only in its reserved linked
worktree after the hook registers the top-level conversation and selected
model ID. Reads are free everywhere. Director seats mutate their worktree
without per-action approval; bound Director/Operator mailbox wrappers inherit
the seat-start grant; every other posture gets one in-app approval per
governed mutation. Remote Git effects always ask.

Default topology is the standing pair (`director` + `operator`). Do not invent
five-seat ceremony; capacity seats stay cold until parallel load earns them.

Use each worktree's native Git index. Never set `GIT_INDEX_FILE` in Cursor app
seats. Preserve unrelated dirty files and stage explicit pathspecs.

Find definitions, writers, callers, imports, and siblings before changing a
symbol. Tests prove only what they execute. Push, merge, lock, and spend are
separate remote effects, each authorized by its own in-app approval. Do not
double-ask in chat after a hook approval for the same command.

Cursor workflow truth lives under `.cursor/` and `docs/protocol/cursor/`. Do not
rewrite Codex/Claude adapters for Cursor-only changes. No Cursor-specific
product destination is currently configured.
